  "question": {
    "text": "The $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\frac{3 x-1}{3 x+1}\\right)^{4 x}$ equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{-8 / 3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{-4 / 9}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\frac{3 x-1}{3 x+1}\\right)^{4 x}=1^{\\infty}=e^{L}=e^{-\\frac{8}{3}}$\r\n$L=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} 4 x\\left(\\frac{3 x-1}{3 x+1}-1\\right)=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} 4 x\\left(\\frac{-2}{3 x+1}\\right)=\\frac{-8}{3}$"
  }
}